# Agent working context: handovers, session logs, audits and browser/diagnostic
# scratch. Kept on disk for coding agents to read, out of the repo because it is
# session history rather than source. AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md deliberately stay
# at the root so they still auto-load.
#
# THE LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. DO NOT REMOVE IT. (2026-09-08)
#
# This was `Agent/`, unanchored, which git matches against a directory of that
# name at ANY depth. On a case-insensitive filesystem - which is every Windows
# and default macOS checkout, and `git config core.ignorecase` is true here -
# that also matches `agent/`. This repository has two of those:
#
#     src/app/agent/           the Expo app's agent detail route
#     web/src/app/agent/       the website's, plus its client half and OG image
#
# So every NEW file under either route was silently untracked. `git add -A`
# reported nothing, `git status` showed nothing, the local build passed because
# the files were on disk - and the Vercel build failed on
# `Can't resolve '@/app/agent/[id]/agent-detail-client'`, because that file had
# never left this machine. Two files were lost this way before it was found.
# `src/app/agent/[id].tsx` and `web/src/app/agent/[id]/page.tsx` survived only
# because they were already tracked, and ignore rules do not apply to files git
# is already following.
#
# `/Agent/` is anchored to this file's directory, so it matches the working
# context at the repository root and nothing nested.
/Agent/

# Installed agent skills, and the lockfile the installer writes beside them.
# `npx skills add` drops a vendored copy of a third-party skill here (and mirrors
# it into Agent/skills/), which is somebody else's documentation rather than this
# project's source - dozens of .md files that would otherwise show up as commit
# candidates on every install. Same reasoning as Agent/ above: kept on disk so
# the skill still loads, out of the repo because it is tooling, not the app.
.agents/
skills-lock.json
# .claude/skills/<name> is a SYMLINK the installer points at .agents/skills/<name>,
# so without this git walks through it and lists every one of the skill's .md
# files a second time. The rest of .claude/ stays tracked - settings.json is real
# project config.
.claude/skills/

# generated native folders
/ios
/android
